    orcid: ""
version: "3.3.10"
date-released: "2025-02-24"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/anuroopshivdasan/LatBOND"
abstract: >-
  LatBOND investigates whether training neural networks under the same latency
  constraints used at deployment significantly outperforms the current practice
  of training without constraints and applying them only at inference time.
  Through a 42-model benchmark across three architectures and five latency
  budgets, we demonstrate that matched training with stepped geometric
  curriculum consistently outperforms truncated training by +0.87 percentage
  points on average.
keywords:
  - automatic music transcription
  - real-time systems
  - onset detection
  - latency constraints
  - distribution shift
  - matched training
  - neural networks
  - curriculum learning
